Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and how they are probably used  

• problem.name : to identify the “problem” (dataset).  
• solution.name / solution.version : to count how many (version – step) rows a problem has in the solution table.  
• model_score.name / model_score.version / model_score.step : to compare the performance of different models (Stack vs. non‑Stack) inside each step of each version.  
• model_score.model : to know if a row is “Stack” or a different model.  
• model_score.test_score : to get the highest non‑Stack test‑score and the Stack test‑score for every (name, version, step).  

Key conditions that will be needed  

1. model_score.model = 'Stack' (Stack rows).  
2. model_score.model <> 'Stack'  (all non‑Stack rows).  
3. For every (name, version, step) :  
   max_non_stack_score < stack_score  
4. Count, over steps 1, 2 and 3, how many times the condition in 3 is true for each problem.  
5. Compare that count to the number of occurrences of the problem in the solution table (across all versions and steps).  
6. Return those problems where the count in 4 is strictly larger than the occurrences counted in 5.  

Ten exploratory → final queries  
(Every query is different; each ends with LIMIT 20)

```sql
-- 1️⃣  Description: List all distinct problems mentioned in the model_score table.
SELECT DISTINCT "name"
FROM "model_score"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2️⃣  Description: Inspect which models exist (so we know whether the literal 'Stack' is present).
SELECT DISTINCT "model"
FROM "model_score"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3️⃣  Description: Show the Stack rows only (to see their test scores).
SELECT "name", "version", "step", "test_score"
FROM   "model_score"
WHERE  "model" = 'Stack'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4️⃣  Description: Show the non‑Stack rows only.
SELECT "name", "version", "step", "model", "test_score"
FROM   "model_score"
WHERE  "model" <> 'Stack'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5️⃣  Description: For every (name,version,step) compute the Stack test score.
SELECT  m1."name",
        m1."version",
        m1."step",
        m1."test_score" AS "stack_test_score"
FROM    "model_score" AS m1
WHERE   m1."model" = 'Stack'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6️⃣  Description: For every (name,version,step) compute the max NON‑Stack test score.
SELECT  m2."name",
        m2."version",
        m2."step",
        MAX(m2."test_score") AS "max_non_stack"
FROM    "model_score" AS m2
WHERE   m2."model" <> 'Stack'
GROUP BY m2."name", m2."version", m2."step"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7️⃣  Description: Put 5 and 6 together to see where max_non_stack < stack_test_score.
SELECT  s."name",
        s."version",
        s."step",
        s."stack_test_score",
        n."max_non_stack"
FROM   (SELECT  "name","version","step","test_score" AS "stack_test_score"
        FROM    "model_score"
        WHERE   "model" = 'Stack')  AS s
JOIN   (SELECT  "name","version","step", MAX("test_score") AS "max_non_stack"
        FROM    "model_score"
        WHERE   "model" <> 'Stack'
        GROUP BY "name","version","step") AS n
  ON  s."name"    = n."name"
  AND s."version" = n."version"
  AND s."step"    = n."step"
WHERE  n."max_non_stack" < s."stack_test_score"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8️⃣  Description: Count, per problem, how many (version,step) rows satisfy the condition above.
WITH better AS (
  SELECT s."name"
  FROM   (SELECT "name","version","step","test_score" AS "stack_test_score"
          FROM   "model_score"
          WHERE  "model"='Stack') AS s
  JOIN   (SELECT "name","version","step", MAX("test_score") AS "max_non_stack"
          FROM   "model_score"
          WHERE  "model" <> 'Stack'
          GROUP BY "name","version","step") AS n
    ON  s."name"    = n."name"
    AND s."version" = n."version"
    AND s."step"    = n."step"
  WHERE n."max_non_stack" < s."stack_test_score"
)
SELECT  "name",
        COUNT(*) AS "cnt_better_than_nonstack"
FROM    better
GROUP BY "name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9️⃣  Description: Count how many total rows a problem has in the solution table (across all versions & steps).
SELECT  "name",
        COUNT(*) AS "cnt_solution_rows"
FROM    "solution"
GROUP BY "name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 🔟  Description: FINAL – return the problems where the #times Stack beats **all** non‑Stack models
--                  (across steps 1,2,3) exceeds the #rows the problem has in solution.
WITH better AS (
  SELECT s."name","version","step"
  FROM   (SELECT "name","version","step","test_score"
          FROM   "model_score"
          WHERE  "model"='Stack') AS s
  JOIN   (SELECT "name","version","step", MAX("test_score") AS "max_non_stack"
          FROM   "model_score"
          WHERE  "model" <> 'Stack'
          GROUP BY "name","version","step") AS n
    ON  s."name"    = n."name"
    AND s."version" = n."version"
    AND s."step"    = n."step"
  WHERE n."max_non_stack" < s."test_score"
),
cnt_better AS (
  SELECT "name", COUNT(*) AS cnt_better
  FROM   better
  GROUP BY "name"
),
cnt_solution AS (
  SELECT "name", COUNT(*) AS cnt_sol
  FROM   "solution"
  GROUP BY "name"
)
SELECT  cb."name"
FROM    cnt_better  AS cb
JOIN    cnt_solution AS cs ON cb."name" = cs."name"
WHERE   cb."cnt_better" > cs."cnt_sol"
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query is limited to 20 rows for safety; remove or raise the LIMIT if you need the full result set.
